From: Naresh Solanki <naresh.solanki.2011@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 23:31:10 +0530
Subject: MIPS: siflower: allow cpufreq, use the DW APB timer

The GIC timer and the CP0 counter both run off the CPU clock, so a CPU
frequency change makes them useless for timekeeping. The SoC's DW APB
timers run from the 100 MHz bus clock. Select DW_APB_TIMER_OF (it has
no prompt), CPU_SUPPORTS_CPUFREQ and MIPS_EXTERNAL_TIMER so cpufreq can
be enabled.

With a DT that declares the timers, the APB timer is the clocksource
and sched_clock; across ~500 frequency changes in 72 s the clock stays
within 0.02% of an external reference.

Signed-off-by: Naresh Solanki <naresh.solanki.2011@gmail.com>
---
 arch/mips/Kconfig | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/mips/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/mips/Kconfig
@@ -948,10 +948,13 @@ config MACH_SIFLOWER_MIPS
 	select COMMON_CLK
 	select CPU_MIPSR2_IRQ_EI
 	select CPU_MIPSR2_IRQ_VI
+	select CPU_SUPPORTS_CPUFREQ
 	select CSRC_R4K
+	select DW_APB_TIMER_OF
 	select DMA_NONCOHERENT
 	select IRQ_MIPS_CPU
 	select MIPS_CPU_SCACHE
+	select MIPS_EXTERNAL_TIMER
 	select MIPS_GIC
 	select MIPS_L1_CACHE_SHIFT_5
 	select NO_EXCEPT_FILL
